Z||000000||William||02-24-2000||12:43 AM||||Anyone know what my chances of finding a Evolution (fiero store) fiero specific cover locally? What do you guys think about the cheaper universal covers? I don't have alot of spare cash right now but need to protect a new paint job imediately. Caught my wifes $%&*& dog sleeping on her firebird's hood!!!! Every day I wait I get more nervous.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||02-24-2000||12:55 AM||||I've bought two here, one from Price Club which is now Sam's or Costco, and one from, I think, Kragen. So they should be around. Watch out for the hole for the antenna. I've ripped mine and had to repair it with felt and fabric spray cement. The cover is kind of a non-woven fabric which tears easily. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||DXR_DAD||02-24-2000||01:03 AM||||Ed, what was the price at Costco? did they only have one style?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||02-24-2000||04:37 AM||||Just unscrew your antenna before you put the cover on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Gokart||02-24-2000||08:52 PM||||Mines a Budget #2. It was only $30.00 and does the job. Had the same prob as Ed and fixed it the same way as Ed! (Great minds think alike). The cover has a cut out for the antenna with extra material to pad around it but gets weak after a while.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Ed||02-24-2000||09:15 PM||||Sorry to be so long to get around to answering, but when you're on the left coast the three hour time difference and work get in the way.<P>When I bought the cover at Price Club it was about $70.  HOWEVER, that was many years ago and I don't shop there anymore.  <P>The Kragen cover cost about $100 as I recall, again, some time ago.<P>One solution to ripping is to remove the antenna before use. That's too much trouble for me. Elaborating on my comments, above, I have reinforced the antenna hole with glued felt, duct tape, and a plastic grommet.  I have to say because its winter, even here in California (!), I haven't tested my fix. ||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||02-24-2000||09:32 PM||||i got my car cover from Kmart, $12....<P>Its thin but does the job I want it to do||||reg||6
